/*  EXPECTED: REJECTED at type-check, identically by both backends.
    A series with no name, sorted out of one made in a rabbit, is handed to a method that keeps it in an
    object outside the rabbit.

    A value with no name was taken to live as long as the program. It lives where it was made, or
    where what it was made from lives, and is judged by that (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, *Open*, closed 2026-11-25). */

Define object bag with (the series of number items).
Bind void to keep unto bag, given (the series of number row):
    One's items becomes row.
Done.
Define b as a new bag { the items a series of number with (9) }.
Pull a rabbit.
    Define xs as a series of number with (3, 2).
    Cast b's keep on (xs sorted).
Done.
State b's items.
